<title>FINLAND: Stockmann rises sharply on H1 report.</title>
<headline>Stockmann rises sharply on H1 report.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish retailer Oy Stockmann Ab rose sharply on Tuesday after the group reported first-half pre-tax earnings rose 46 percent to 162 million markka, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0935 GMT, Stockmann traded at 289.00, up 17.00 markka or more than six percent, after briefly touching 300.00. Volume was fair at five million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;The result was better than expected, even though it contained some gains on asset sales,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
